content.text:
The Pipeline already records the PR-head SHA immediately after checkout and has one outer `finally` block, so status reporting can be added without changing the parameterized job or SLURM behavior:

- post `pending` after the trusted checkout identifies the SHA;
- post `success`, `failure`, or `error` after the build’s cleanup/archival path;
- use the current username/password credential’s token only inside the short API-call step, never while PR code is executing.

I recommend the stable GitHub context `continuous-integration/jenkins/stellar-intel`. The only remaining policy choice is how strongly a GitHub API outage should affect Jenkins.

